---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../data/site';

const effectiveDate = 'Effective August 7, 2026';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of use | Creaturely"
  description="Terms for using the Creaturely animal health journal, including the veterinary disclaimer and open-source license."
  heading="Terms that respect the purpose of the tool."
  intro="Creaturely helps you keep your own records. It does not replace professional veterinary care or make medical decisions."
  effectiveDate={effectiveDate}
>
  <nav slot="contents">
    <a href="#agreement">Agreement</a>
    <a href="#journal">The journal</a>
    <a href="#medical">Veterinary disclaimer</a>
    <a href="#your-content">Your information</a>
    <a href="#backups">Backups and services</a>
    <a href="#open-source">Open source</a>
    <a href="#availability">Availability</a>
    <a href="#liability">Liability</a>
    <a href="#changes">Changes and contact</a>
  </nav>

  <section id="agreement">
    <h2>Agreement</h2>
    <p>
      These terms apply when you use the Creaturely mobile application or this website. By using
      Creaturely, you agree to use it lawfully and in a way that does not interfere with other
      people, systems, or services.
    </p>
    <p>If you do not agree with these terms, do not use Creaturely.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="journal">
    <h2>What Creaturely provides</h2>
    <p>
      Creaturely is a free, local-first journal for information you choose to record about animals
      in your care. Features can include profiles, observations, measurements, medication records,
      reminders, documents, trends, exports, and backups.
    </p>
    <p>
      You are responsible for deciding what to enter, checking its accuracy, and keeping any copies
      you need. Creaturely does not verify user-entered information.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="medical">
    <h2>Veterinary and safety disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      Creaturely is not a diagnostic tool, medical device, emergency service, or substitute for a
      veterinarian. It does not diagnose, predict, treat, or confirm the health of an animal.
    </p>
    <p>
      Measurements, trends, and reminders are record-keeping aids. They can be incomplete,
      delayed, or affected by how information was entered. If you are worried about an animal,
      contact a veterinarian. For an urgent concern, use an appropriate veterinary emergency
      service rather than relying on the app or a notification.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="your-content">
    <h2>Your information and responsibilities</h2>
    <p>
      You retain responsibility for the journal content, photos, and documents you add. Only add
      information that you have the right to store and share. Protect the device and any exported
      copies in a way that fits the sensitivity of the information.
    </p>
    <p>
      Do not post real animal health records, personal documents, or Creaturely backups in public
      support issues. Use synthetic or carefully redacted examples when reporting a problem.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="backups">
    <h2>Backups, exports, and third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      System share sheets, file providers, Apple CloudKit, Google Drive, GitHub, app stores, and
      other external services are operated by their respective providers. Their availability,
      security, and terms are outside Creaturely's control.
    </p>
    <p>
      Test important backups before depending on them. Keep more than one copy when the record
      matters. Optional cloud recovery is not a promise of continuous sync or permanent storage.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="open-source">
    <h2>Open-source license</h2>
    <p>
      Creaturely's source code is free software under the GNU General Public License version 3.
      Your rights to copy, study, modify, and distribute the software are governed by that license,
      which is available in the <a href={siteConfig.licenseUrl}>public repository</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Creaturely name, logos, and other brand assets are not automatically licensed for use as
      the identity of a different product merely because the application code is open source.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="availability">
    <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
    <p>
      Creaturely may change as the project develops. Features can be added, revised, or removed,
      and support for operating-system versions can change. There is no guarantee that every
      feature will always be available on every device.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="liability">
    <h2>Warranty and liability</h2>
    <p>
      Creaturely is provided without warranties to the extent permitted by law. Vector42 does not
      guarantee that the software will be uninterrupted, error-free, or suitable for a particular
      medical, legal, or record-retention purpose.
    </p>
    <p>
      To the extent permitted by law, Vector42 is not liable for indirect, incidental, special, or
      consequential loss arising from use of Creaturely, reliance on reminders or records, loss of
      local data, or use of an external service. Rights that cannot legally be excluded remain in
      effect.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes">
    <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>
      These terms may be updated as Creaturely changes. A revised effective date will appear at the
      top of this page.
    </p>
    <p>
      Questions can be submitted through the <a href={siteConfig.supportUrl}>Creaturely support form</a>.
      Remember that GitHub issues are public.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
